% A child's ABO blood group follows from one allele of each parent. A, B and
% O are the alleles; A and B are dominant over O and codominant with each
% other. From the blood types a test observes, the program works out the
% genotypes a person can have, the blood types a child of two people can have,
% and which men a child's blood type excludes as its father.
% Lucas, type B, cannot be the son of Maria, type A, and Tom, type O: Tom is
% excluded and Sam and Ken are not. Eva, type O, excludes Sam, type AB.
% Shows alternative rules for dominance, genotypes enumerated from a list of
% alleles, possibility through every combination of the parents' alleles, and
% an exclusion as "it is not the case that" over all of them.
% After Landsteiner's ABO blood group system and its Mendelian inheritance.

the templates are:
    *an allele* is an ABO allele,
    *an allele* is dominant over *an allele*,
    the alleles *an allele* and *an allele* give blood type *a type*,
    *a person* has blood type *a type*,
    *a person* can have the alleles *an allele* and *an allele*,
    a child of *a mother* and *a father* can have blood type *a type*,
    *a person* is the mother of *a child*,
    *a person* is male,
    *a man* is excluded as the father of *a child*.

the knowledge base abo inheritance includes:

A is an ABO allele.
B is an ABO allele.
O is an ABO allele.
A is dominant over O.
B is dominant over O.

% Two equal alleles give their own type; a dominant allele hides a recessive
% one; A and B together give AB.
the alleles an allele X and X give blood type X
    if X is an ABO allele.

the alleles an allele X and an allele Y give blood type X
    if X is dominant over Y.

the alleles an allele X and an allele Y give blood type Y
    if Y is dominant over X.

the alleles A and B give blood type AB.

the alleles B and A give blood type AB.

% A blood type allows each genotype that gives it.
a person can have the alleles an allele X and an allele Y
    if the person has blood type a type
    and X is an ABO allele
    and Y is an ABO allele
    and the alleles X and Y give blood type the type.

% A child takes one allele of each parent's genotype.
a child of a mother and a father can have blood type a type
    if the mother can have the alleles an allele M1 and an allele M2
    and the father can have the alleles an allele F1 and an allele F2
    and an allele X is in [M1, M2]
    and an allele Y is in [F1, F2]
    and the alleles X and Y give blood type the type.

% A man is excluded when no genotype of his, with any of the mother's,
% gives the child's blood type.
a man is excluded as the father of a child
    if a mother is the mother of the child
    and the child has blood type a type
    and the man is male
    and the man has blood type a second type
    and it is not the case that
        a child of the mother and the man can have blood type the type.

scenario paternity is:
    Maria has blood type A.
    Lucas has blood type B.
    Eva has blood type O.
    Maria is the mother of Lucas.
    Maria is the mother of Eva.
    Tom is male.
    Sam is male.
    Ken is male.
    Tom has blood type O.
    Sam has blood type AB.
    Ken has blood type B.
    mother expects answers ["Maria can have the alleles A and A", "Maria can have the alleles A and O",
        "Maria can have the alleles O and A"].
    sam expects answers ["Sam can have the alleles A and B", "Sam can have the alleles B and A"].
    children expects answers ["a child of Maria and Tom can have blood type A",
        "a child of Maria and Tom can have blood type O"].
    excluded expects answers ["Tom is excluded as the father of Lucas", "Sam is excluded as the father of Eva"].

query mother is:
    Maria can have the alleles which allele and which other allele.

query sam is:
    Sam can have the alleles which allele and which other allele.

query children is:
    a child of Maria and Tom can have blood type which type.

query excluded is:
    which man is excluded as the father of which child.
